@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Proposed — Authentication and conditional second factor
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

actor User
participant "Trusted login entry" as E
participant "Identity owner" as I
participant "Evaluated credential / factor mechanism" as V
database "Current account / session state" as D
User -> E : selected login proof over protected transport
E -> I : validated bounded authentication request
I -> V : verify actual required primary proof
V --> I : actual verified / failed / unavailable result
alt valid proof and eligible current account
 opt accepted policy requires additional factor / step-up
  I -> V : verify scoped second-factor proof
  V --> I : verified / failed / unavailable
 end
 I -> D : establish fresh session only if every required proof succeeded\nand current account remains eligible
 D --> I : actual session context or refusal
 I --> E : protected session result / safe failure
else failed / unavailable / ineligible
 I --> E : safe generic refusal; no bypass
end
E --> User : actual authentication result
note over E,D
 No passwords, factor values or raw session IDs in ordinary logs.
 Concrete fixation, cookie, CSRF, throttling and factor mechanisms need evaluation.
end note

@enduml
